<title>INDIA: Indian Jan industrial output up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Indian Jan industrial output up 1.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's index of industrial production increased by 1.1 percent in January over the same month in 1996, the government said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Between April 1996 and January 1997, the index increased 7.5 percent over the same 10-month period from April 1995 to January 1996, it said.  </p>
<p>    INDUSTRIAL PRODUCTION     Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	  +1.1	+4.0     +12.9</p>
<p>     -Mining			 -1.3	+0.2	+4.9</p>
<p>     -Manufacturing		+0.9	+4.6     +15.4</p>
<p>     -Electricity		  +4.2	+3.7	+6.6</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1980/81)  315.7     318.8     312.4</p>
<p>Note - Figures for January 1997 are preliminary. Figures for December 1996 have been revised.  </p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    CUMULATIVE		   Apr 96-Jan 97   Apr 95-Jan 96</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	    +7.5	     +11.7</p>
<p>     -Mining			   +1.4		+7.8</p>
<p>     -Manufacturing		  +9.0	     +12.8</p>
<p>     -Electricity		    +3.8		+8.6</p>
<p>     Index (base 100=1980/81)   296.7	     276.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures for January 1997 are preliminary.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
